{#- N2/N6. The whole Cost Watch list, at full width. Same header pattern and
    pageId as /news/, so the export's page-scoped news rules apply unchanged.

    N6: the items are now the same card as an Uncost update — publisher and
    date on the eyebrow row, the claim as the body, the outbound link and the
    single Reported label in the foot — run one-up down the page instead of
    two-up in a rail. Nothing is summarised for them: the claim IS the summary.

    The Reported definition used to print twice on this page, once in the
    column head and once inside the block below it. It prints once now, folded
    into the cross-reference block at the top — the one place on the page that
    tells a reader where they are and what the label means.

    It is still deliberately NOT added to the four-label confidence block on
    /case/ or /receipts/: Reported is not a confidence value: it says a source
    published a figure, not that we verified one. -#}
<!-- SECTION: news-cost-watch.Cost Watch — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="Cost Watch — title"><h1>Cost <span class="u-1">Watch</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>Cost Watch</h2>
  <p>Prices in the news, with the publisher and the date attached. Not receipts &mdash; verified figures live in <a href="/receipts/">The Receipts</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="newswrap newswrap--solo">
  <!-- SECTION: news-cost-watch.Cost Watch -->
  <div class="costwatch" data-screen-label="Cost Watch">
    <div class="newsxref">
      <p>For Uncost&rsquo;s own updates, see <a href="/news/">the news</a>.</p>
      <p class="newsxref-def"><b>Reported</b> &mdash; a price or cost figure as published by the linked source, with its date. Cost Watch is a watch list, not a receipt; verified figures live in <a href="/receipts/">The Receipts</a>.</p>
    </div>
{#- N5 keyword filter, same progressive-enhancement pattern as /receipts/: the
    bar ships hidden and only /js/keyword-filter.js reveals it, so with JS off
    every item renders and no dead control is shown. -#}
    <div class="rfilter" data-keyword-filter data-filter-for="news-costwatch" data-filter-noun="items" hidden>
      <label for="cfilter-q">Filter these items</label>
      <input id="cfilter-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try &ldquo;gasoline&rdquo; or &ldquo;BLS&rdquo;&hellip;">
      <span class="rfilter-count" data-filter-count></span>
    </div>
    <div id="news-costwatch" class="cwlist">
{% for row in register.newsFeed %}
      {{ nc.costwatch(row) }}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="u-97">Checked {{ register.lastChecked }}. Every figure here has a <a href="/receipts/#register">receipt</a>. Prefer a feed? <a href="/news/cost-watch/feed.xml">Subscribe by RSS</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
